Package: gsipper
Version: __VERSION__
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: __ARCH__
Maintainer: pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/pulpoff/gsipper
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10),
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1,
         gir1.2-gsound-1.0,
         sound-theme-freedesktop
Recommends: gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1,
            gnome-shell-extension-prefs
Suggests: python3-pjsua2
Description: Modern GNOME SIP client
 gsipper is a Python / GTK4 / libadwaita SIP softphone for the
 GNOME desktop, in the spirit of MicroSIP. It supports outgoing
 and incoming calls, a contacts list (with vCard and Google CSV
 import), per-contact call history, SIP instant messaging and
 a top-bar status indicator via a bundled GNOME Shell extension.
 .
 The PJSUA2 Python bindings are not packaged on Debian/Ubuntu.
 After installing this package, run:
   sudo gsipper --install-pjsua2
 to compile them from source (~5 min, ~150 MB cache under
 ~/.cache/gsipper/pjproject-2.14.1). The cache is reused across
 reinstalls and is left in place on package removal.
